<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>at the moment i am ready for trial tests, i have one question about stack, stack frame needs to be prepared?<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>asm volatile ("push r4-r11\n""subi sp, sp, 0x14\n""stw r1, (sp, 0x0C)\n""movi r1, 0x00002000\n""stw r1, (sp, 0x08)\n""movi r1, 1\n""stw r1, (sp, 0x04)\n""movi r1, 0x00000800\n""stw r1, (sp, 0x00)\n""movi r3, 0x50\n""movi r1, 0\n""jsri " QU(AMBE_ENCODE)"addi sp, sp, 0x14\n""pop r4-r11");</code></pre></div></div></blockquote>This assembler code calls the function and passes a pointer to a buffer, and probably some other parameters<br><br>Someone posted a pure C version of this to the forum, but we did not use it because I think it caused the code size to increase <br><br>However you should probably use the C version, because this would be easier than porting the ARM code to CSky</div></blockquote>this is already code for C-SKY, it just often uses the stack to store variables and you may have to make a copy of the stack<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6341">R3MDG</a> — Tue Jun 03, 2025 2:19 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
